17 false] [17592186092264 1038 17592186526015 13194139535680 17592186045417 true] [17592186092264 1038 17592186526078 13194139535680 17592186045417 true] [17592186092265 1038 17592186525997 13194139535680 17592186045417 true] [17592186092417 1050 540.0 13194139535680 17592186045417 true] [17592186092732 1070 17592186045485 13194139535680 17592186045417 true] [17592186092732 1071 "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y={log}_{3}⁡(5x-2).$" 13194139535680 17592186045417 true] [17592186092732 1071 "Calculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ for $y = \\log_{3} (5x - 2)$." 13194139535680 17592186045417 false] [17592186092732 1074 "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={log}_{3}⁡(u),\\,u=5x-2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(5x-2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{(5x-2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535680 17592186045417 true] [17592186093370 1064 "The chain rule can be used to differentiate logarithmic functions like \n\n$$\ny = \\ln (2x+1).\n$$\n\nFirst notice that this function can be written as the composite function\n\n$$\ny = \\ln u, \\qquad u = 2x+1.\n$$\n\nWe can use the chain rule to compute the derivative of this composite function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}u)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{u}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $u=2x+1,$ we obtain the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{2x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535680 17592186045417 false] [17592186093370 1064 "The chain rule can be used to differentiate logarithmic functions like \n\n$$\ny = \\ln (2x+1).\n$$\n\nFirst notice that this function can be written as the composite function\n\n$$\ny = \\ln u, \\qquad u = 2x+1.\n$$\n\nWe can use the chain rule to compute the derivative of this composite function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{u}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $u=2x+1,$ we obtain the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{2x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535680 17592186045417 true] [17592186094915 1075 17592186094916 13194139535680 17592186045417 false] [17592186094915 1075 17592186094917 13194139535680 17592186045417 false] [17592186094915 1075 17592186094918 13194139535680 17592186045417 false] [17592186094915 1075 17592186094919 13194139535680 17592186045417 false] [17592186094915 1075 17592186094920 13194139535680 17592186045417 false] [17592186094915 1075 17592186525302 13194139535680 17592186045417 true] [17592186094915 1075 17592186525474 13194139535680 17592186045417 true] [17592186094915 1075 17592186525643 13194139535680 17592186045417 true] [17592186094915 1075 17592186525763 13194139535680 17592186045417 true] [17592186094915 1075 17592186525775 13194139535680 17592186045417 true] [17592186094915 1078 17592186525763 13194139535680 17592186045417 true] [17592186096416 1074 "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left( \\log_4 x + \\ln x \\right)\\\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\log_4 x) 