atorname{ln}⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(\\frac{4}{x}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2))|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535680 17592186045417 true] [17592186314912 1074 "To find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4ln⁡x-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{x}+5) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{x}ln⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(\\frac{4}{x}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{x}ln⁡(2))|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{2}ln⁡(2) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{4}{3}ln⁡(2)\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535680 17592186045417 false] [17592186332657 1071 "![](images/22/22505181ad0a10e74a158edabc949444055f1deda57286ff63674c32f2dc79c7.png)\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the point $P$ on the curve $y={log}_{2}⁡x$  that is closest to the origin (as shown above) satisfies the equation \n\n$$\n2x+=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139535680 17592186045417 false] [17592186332657 1071 "![](images/22/22505181ad0a10e74a158edabc949444055f1deda57286ff63674c32f2dc79c7.png)\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the point $P$ on the curve $y={log}_{2}⁡x$  that is closest to the origin (as shown above) satisfies the equation \n\n$$\n2x+\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAAA}}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139535680 17592186045417 true] [17592186339124 1071 "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[0,1]$\n\n- 